      "ground_truth": "Returns non-overlapping intervals covering the input; overlapping and touching intervals (shared endpoint) merge.",
      "golden_response": "Reference approach (passes all 9 cases):\n\n```python\nclass Solution:\n    def merge(self, intervals: list[list[int]]) -> list[list[int]]:\n        intervals.sort()\n        out = [intervals[0][:]]\n        for s, e in intervals[1:]:\n            if s <= out[-1][1]:\n                out[-1][1] = max(out[-1][1], e)\n            else:\n                out.append([s, e])\n        return out\n```",
